# dt2w_uewake — gesture-node arming actions (vendor_init half).
#
# Installed to /odm so these builtin `write` actions run in the vendor_init
# domain, which the stock vendor policy already allows to write the vendor-
# labelled (syna_proc) node /proc/touchscreen/wake_gesture. The coredomain
# daemon (service block in dt2w_uewake.rc on /system_ext) cannot touch syna_proc,
# so it pulses sys.dt2w.arm 0->1 and the action below does the real write on each
# 0->1 transition. The disable path also clears the arm here (vendor_init).
#
# NOTE: this file carries NO `service` block — the service is declared on
# /system_ext so init's coredomain transition fires. Keeping a service block here
# would (a) leave the daemon in u:r:init:s0 and (b) collide with the system_ext
# definition. When this lands, BOTH odm and system_ext must be flashed (the old
# odm .rc + old /odm/bin/dt2w_uewake binary must be removed).

on property:persist.sys.dt2w.enabled=0
    write /proc/touchscreen/wake_gesture 0

# Daemon-requested re-arm (vendor_init writes the vendor syna_proc node).
on property:sys.dt2w.arm=1
    write /proc/touchscreen/wake_gesture 1
